Expected elements: MISSING — a timeline or scrubber expressing position within the trace.

That is finding #1, it is P1, and it caps the rating at 4. The identity bar carries the stepping toolbar, the phase rail and the fraction `128 / 1315`, but there is no tick strip, track or any spatial expression of where step 128 sits inside 1315 — the bar goes straight from the last button group to the numeric readout. A fraction is a readout, not a timeline; the must-show lists both.

On density otherwise: the pane row gets 654 of 900 px because the provenance banner takes 180 px (20% of the viewport) to set four lines of prose across only the left 41% of the width — 850×120 px of that band is empty, and those rows come out of the register's scarcest resource. The measurement the change had not made: the Call Trace region is 389 px tall, its seven frames and the "By call order." footer end at ~508, leaving ~127 px (33%) empty, while the Values pane directly below it is cut mid-row at the fold with more values underneath. The height is in the wrong half of that column. The Code pane meanwhile clips lines 26, 40–44 mid-identifier at its right edge, and clips a `+3` value chip, with no scrollbar.

Highest-priority fixes: restore a position expression at ≤1780 px, and move ~120 px from the call-trace region to Values.

Rating: 4/10

